{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>No, my bones</b> — the generative power that is not seen and has not emerged into act, like the power of the elder in the young child, and speech in the newborn. And if it is hidden from the sight of the eye, even from the sight of the eye of the heart it is not hidden from You; from the root it is not hidden from Adonai." "<b>I was made</b> — from the root of מעשה (deed/making), not from the root of ועסותם רשעים (and the wicked plot). And there [too] is [the root of] עשו דדי בתוליהן (their breasts grew firm)." "<b>And the meaning of רקמתי (I was embroidered)</b> — it is the form that emerges into actuality. Rabbi Moses said: because David spoke against the first father [Adam] who was created from the earth, therefore he said: 'I was embroidered in the lowest parts of the earth.' And in my opinion: he speaks of himself, and likens the hidden places of the womb to the hidden places of the lowest parts of the earth. And behold, regarding the creatures it is written: 'and behold a wheel below,' corresponding to wheels above it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {1 "The phrase ועסותם רשעים likely alludes to a verse or rabbinic dictum involving the root עס\"י in the sense of plotting/acting; the precise reference is uncertain.", 2 "The final sentence quotes Ezekiel's vision language ('והנה אופן שפל') by way of analogy; the application to the psalm verse is characteristically compressed and left as stated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:17.264761839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}